course: dictionary
lesson: 891
title: Birthday and the clues around it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A birthday is the day each year when a person was born. Birthday can be a noun, as in «her birthday», or it can come before another noun, as in «birthday cake» or «birthday card». The word after birthday tells you what kind of thing it is.
explain: «Lily invited girls from both streets to her birthday, and her mum had to buy twice as many party bags.» The party bags are the clue. A birthday party is a party for someone's birthday, with guests and treats. Read the words around birthday and its meaning becomes clear.
explain: Small words give clues too. «A boy in Arizona wants a bearded dragon for his birthday» uses for to show the gift is for the occasion. «On my birthday» and «for her birthday» show when or why something happens, so always check the words next to the word you are learning.
fact: A birthday is the day each year when a person was born.
fact: «Birthday» can be a noun, as in «her birthday», or come before a noun, as in «birthday cake» and «birthday card».
fact: Birthdays often bring gifts, cakes, balloons and parties.
fact: Each birthday a person is one year older.
fact: «Happy birthday» is what people say to wish someone well on their birthday.
exercise: «Lily invited girls from both streets to her birthday.» What is a birthday? | A card with a message inside | A street with lots of houses | A kind of party game | *The day each year when a person was born
exercise: In «birthday cake», what does birthday tell you about the cake? | *A cake for a birthday party | A cake that is very old | A cake that is cold and wet | A cake with a red birthday card
exercise: «Each birthday a person is one year older.» What happens each birthday? | *The person gets one year older | The person stops growing | The person goes to school for the first time | The person moves house
test: «Charles became King on 6 May 2023, which was also Harry's son Archie's birthday.» On what day was Archie's birthday? | 1500 | 1982 | 1147 | *6 May 2023
test: Ella's friend says «happy birthday» to her. What does this mean? | An order to be quiet | A question about what day it is | A warning that rain is coming | *A wish of good cheer for someone on their birthday
exam: «Lily's mum had to buy twice as many party bags for her birthday.» What does «for her birthday» tell you? | *It tells you the occasion, the birthday the party is for | It tells you the bags are broken | It tells you the colour of the bags | It tells you where the bags were made
